01:40.000 --> 01:44.000
May 5th is a day of remembrance.

01:44.000 --> 01:47.000
It's a kind of a veteran's day
in the Netherlands.

01:49.000 --> 01:54.000
And it follows right on the
heels of May 4th, where at 8
p.m. in the evening.

01:54.000 --> 01:58.000
And this is actually a pretty
interesting culture of
phenomenon in the Netherlands.

01:58.000 --> 02:02.000
May 4th at 8 o'clock in the
evening, all church bells across
the country start to ring.

02:02.000 --> 02:06.000
And there's two minutes of
silence to remember the dead,

02:06.000 --> 02:12.000
and also not just those who,
well, to remember World War II.

02:12.000 --> 02:17.000
That's really it. So it's not
just, you know, victims on any
on forces.

02:18.000 --> 02:24.000
And of course, the Netherlands
lost millions of Jews to German
concentration camps.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.000
But it's great to see this.

02:25.000 --> 02:29.000
What happens at 8 p.m. all
television stops.

02:29.000 --> 02:30.000
All radio stops.

02:30.000 --> 02:33.000
